## TypeScript End-User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive, robust, and  TypeScript-friendly for controlling 3D camera animations, balancing ease of use with comprehensive functionality.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:** The central hub managing all camera animation actions. Instances represent individual cameras within your scene.

   ```typescript
   import { AnimationTimeline, EaseFunction } from './animationUtils'; // Hypothetical utility module

   export class CameraController {
     private _target: THREE.Object3D; // Target object the camera orbits/tracks
     private _position: THREE.Vector3;
     private _rotation: THREE.Euler;
     private _animationTimeline: AnimationTimeline; // Manages keyframe animations

     constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, target: THREE.Object3D) {
       this._target = target;
       this._position = new THREE.Vector3(); // Initial position (settable)
       this._rotation = new THREE.Euler(); // Initial rotation (settable)
       this._animationTimeline = new AnimationTimeline(); 
     }

     // Public API Methods:
     setOrbitParams(radius: number, theta: number, phi: number) {
       this._position.setFromSphericalCoords(radius, theta, phi); // Update orbital parameters
     }

     setPosition(position: THREE.Vector3) {  this._position = position; }
     setRotation(rotation: THREE.Euler) { this._rotation = rotation; }

     /** Animation Functions - Keyframe Based */
     addKeyframePosition(time: number, pos: THREE.Vector3) {
       this._animationTimeline.addKeyframe('position', time, pos);
     }
     addKeyframeRotation(time: number, rot: THREE.Euler) {
       this._animationTimeline.addKeyframe('rotation', time, rot);
     }
     animate(duration: number, easing: EaseFunction = 'linear') {
       this._animationTimeline.animate(duration, easing); // Drives camera updates
     }

     // ... (Additional methods for smooth transitions, presets, constraints, etc.)
   }
   ```

2. **`AnimationTimeline` (Utility Class):** Handles interpolation and playback of keyframe data, providing flexibility

```dart
import 'dart:collection';

class Transaction {
  final String coinName;
  final DateTime dateTime;
  final double profitLoss; // Positive for profit, negative for loss

  Transaction({required this.coinName, required this.dateTime, required this.profitLoss});
}

Future<Map<String, dynamic>> analyzeTransactions(List<Transaction> transactions) async {
  // Group transactions by coin name for aggregation
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((t) => t.coinName);

  // Calculate average profit/loss per coin
  final avgProfits = <String, double>{};
  final avgLosses = <String, double>{};
  for (var (coin, coinTransactions) in groupedTransactions.entries) {
    double totalProfit = 0;
    double totalLoss = 0;
    for (var transaction in coinTransactions) {
      totalProfit += transaction.profitLoss;
      totalLoss -= transaction.profitLoss; // Invert for loss calculation
    }
    avgProfits[coin] = totalProfit / coinTransactions.length;
    avgLosses[coin] = totalLoss / coinTransactions.length;
  }

  // Extract top 3 with highest average profit and loss
  final topProfits = avgProfits.entries.toList()
    ..sort((a, b) => b.value.compareTo(a.value)) // Descending order
    ..take(3)
    .toMap(); // Convert back to Map for clarity

  final topLosses = avgLosses.entries.toList()
    ..sort((a, b) => a.value.compareTo(b.value)) // Ascending order for losses
    ..take(3)
    .toMap();

  return {'topProfits': topProfits, 'topLosses': topLosses};
}

// Example Usage (assuming you have populated 'transactions' list)
analyzeTransactions(transactions).then((result) {
  print("Top 3 Profitable Coins: ${result['topProfits']}");
  print("Top 3 Losing Coins: ${result['topLosses']}");
});
```

